# Udev rules for device-mapper devices.
#
# These rules are responsible for sending a notification to a process
# waiting for completion of udev rules. The process is identified by
# a cookie value sent within "change" and "remove" events (the cookie
# value is set before by that process for every action requested).
#
# LeakSanitizer performs its exit-time leak check by starting a helper that
# uses ptrace to suspend and inspect the terminating process.  Programs run by
# systemd-udevd execute in a restricted worker context where this ptrace attach
# can fail with EPERM.  LSan then terminates dmsetup with an error even though
# the udev cookie was completed successfully, which can leave the waiting LVM
# command reporting a spurious udev failure.  Disable only leak detection for
# this short-lived helper; AddressSanitizer and UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer
# checks remain enabled while dmsetup is running.

ENV{DM_COOKIE}=="?*", ENV{LSAN_OPTIONS}="detect_leaks=0", RUN+="(DM_EXEC)/dmsetup udevcomplete $env{DM_COOKIE}"
